id: story-of-scripture
title: The Story of Scripture
version: 1
creator: Day by Word
summary: The story the Bible tells, from its first chapters to its last, in
  51 readings of narrative passages chosen where the story turns: the
  beginning, Israel's ancestors, the exodus and Sinai, the land and the
  kings, exile and return, the life, death and resurrection of Jesus as the
  Gospels tell it, the first churches, and the Bible's last two chapters.
suits: Readers who want the Bible's story as a whole before reading whole
  books, in readings of about 4 or 5 minutes on five days a week.
schedule: sequence
behaviors: pace, finish-date
reading-days: 5
coverage: selection
canon: protestant
books: GEN, EXO, NUM, DEU, JOS, JDG, RUT, 1SA, 2SA, 1KI, 2KI, EZR, NEH,
  DAN, MAT, MRK, LUK, JHN, ACT, REV
limitations: It is a selection made by Day by Word: it reads passages from
  20 books and leaves out most of each, and it reads no psalms, wisdom
  books or letters, and none of the prophets' oracles. Another selection
  could tell the story with other passages; this one follows the narrative
  and makes no claim that its passages matter more than others. It is an
  introduction, not a substitute for reading whole books. Its readings
  differ in length, from about 2 minutes to about 13.
instructions: Read the next reading on each of your five reading days, in
  any Bible; the other two days of the week are rest days. If you miss a
  day, your next reading waits for you. At five readings a week the plan
  takes about eleven weeks.
source: An original selection by Day by Word: narrative passages in the
  order the story unfolds, which is mostly the order the books are
  printed, chosen at its turning points and mostly whole chapters.
  Choosing them is editorial judgment, made for a first introduction; the
  plan names its passages and nothing more. Reading times are estimated
  from word counts of the World English Bible, a public-domain
  translation; the plan can be read in any translation.
rights: daybyword-original
review: reviewed
